WEBVTT

NOTE
This file was generated by Descript <www.descript.com>

00:00:00.380 --> 00:00:03.780
JOE: Many children on the autism
spectrum are dependent on prompts

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:08.480
provided by adults for staying on-task,
completing activities and transitioning

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:11.989
between activities in the home,
school and community environments.

00:00:12.719 --> 00:00:15.739
But over reliance on prompting
should be avoided as this can

00:00:15.740 --> 00:00:17.650
become habit-forming in itself.

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:21.370
BETH: Prompt dependency can be recognised
when the individual is not prepared

00:00:21.370 --> 00:00:24.950
for anything, such as getting dressed
and ready to start the day, and they

00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:27.040
are relying on being told what to do.

00:00:27.179 --> 00:00:31.230
To reduce or prevent prompt dependency
there should always be a plan made for

00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:36.369
fading it out and from the outset plans
should be set up to implement fading once

00:00:36.380 --> 00:00:38.280
the behaviour has become more regulated.

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:41.250
JOE: By reducing prompts and
only using them when needed

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:43.480
the dependency can be reduced.

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:47.790
In the beginning using prompts can
help with all steps of a process,

00:00:48.139 --> 00:00:51.650
but as time progresses an individual
should be encouraged to organise

00:00:51.650 --> 00:00:55.080
their own checklist, getting them
to try to figure things out more.

00:00:55.750 --> 00:00:58.220
BETH: This can be done by
telling them to get dressed but

00:00:58.220 --> 00:00:59.860
leaving them to choose the steps.

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:04.039
This can then be expanded to what to
do to start the day, such as ‘it’s

00:01:04.039 --> 00:01:07.569
time to get up and get ready’ and
the rest is up to them following

00:01:07.570 --> 00:01:09.349
their own checklist or timetable.

00:01:09.759 --> 00:01:13.539
JOE: It’s a gradual process to move
an individual from intense prompt

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:17.700
dependence to self-sufficiency and
as this process begins, there should

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:21.700
be time factored in to encourage
the thinking process, rather than

00:01:21.730 --> 00:01:23.530
immediately correcting the individual.

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:28.030
BETH: There is no one way of breaking
prompt dependency in autism, and

00:01:28.039 --> 00:01:31.860
any changes a parent or carer
makes will probably reflect in the

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:33.869
behaviour of the child or individual.

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:38.140
However, the goal in every instance
is to encourage the individual

00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:41.410
with autism to become more
independent in problem solving.

